 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-005\",\n \"clauses\": {\"identify\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Look at the shapes in different sizes and orientations. Which shape on the board has {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 is the only family that asks the learner to identify a shape. Its v slot draws one of three identification clues, and the keyed answer is derived from question (F07), so a learner identifies a named shape from its edges.\"},\n  \"simple_2_dimensional_shapes\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Look at the shapes in different sizes and orientations. Which shape on the board has {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 presents the board of shapes and asks which one matches a clue. The bank draws triangle, square and rectangle answers, so the shapes addressed are the 2-dimensional shapes named in the competency.\"},\n  \"triangle\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"{answer}\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 prints the answer from _ITEM_POOL, and the bank has triangle rows (for example the first row). F03 adds a hint about triangles.\"},\n  \"rectangle\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"{answer}\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 prints the answer from _ITEM_POOL, and the bank has rectangle rows. The v clue two longer and two shorter straight edges in F06 is the rectangle clue, but that clue is the part of F06 at fault.\"},\n  \"square\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"{answer}\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 prints the answer from _ITEM_POOL, and the bank has square rows. F02 adds a hint about squares.\"},\n  \"different_size\": {\"verdict\": \"NOT_PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": null, \"template\": null, \"reasoning\": \"The packet declares no size variant and no family slot whose domain varies size. The F06 sentence about different sizes only asserts the size on the board; no declared domain or variant produces a size difference.\"},\n  \"different_orientation\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Look at the shapes in different sizes and orientations. Which shape on the board has {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The declared variant orientation with values rotated and standard is used by F07 (derived_from_values includes orientation), and F06 names orientations to the learner.\"}\n },\n \"failing_families\": [\"F06\"],\n \"failing_templates\": [\"Look at the shapes in different sizes and orientations. Which shape on the board has {v}?\"],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"F06 at fault: its v domain (the three identification clues) includes the clue two longer and two shorter straight edges, which asks the learner to compare edge lengths. The vocabulary word length is in NOT_YET_KNOWN, so length comparison is a measurement concept beyond this lc's gate, and it is not in cumulative_vocab. F01 to F05 and F07 to F08 pass: F01 to F04 use only straight edges, side is gated out, and the sentences are correct for a triangle, square and rectangle; F05 prints option letters A to D that match the four options; F07 and F08 print bank shape names only, with none of these as a fixed distractor, and no printed text uses a NOT_YET_KNOWN word. The F06 v clue four equal straight edges and three straight edges match the square and triangle rows, but the packet's domains do not show that the keyed answer is tied to v beyond the generator's claim in F07 derived_from_values.\"}",
